Q6
a) What time complexity do you expect?

Expected complexity:
Θ(nlogn)

Reason:

Building the PQ by n inserts: each insert is
O(logn) ⇒ total O(nlogn)

Removing min n times: each removeMin is
O(logn) ⇒ totalO(nlogn)

So PQSort overall is:
O(nlogn)+O(nlogn)=O(nlogn)

b) What do you find?

When you print time/(n log2 n) (the “ratio” column), if the algorithm is truly nlogn,
that ratio should be roughly constant as n grows (it won’t be perfectly constant because of cache/memory/JVM effects).